 """A binary classifier. eval.py calls fit(X, y) on the training split and predict(model, X) on new rows.
 
 X is a float array of shape (n, 16), y is 0/1 of shape (n,). numpy is the only dependency available.
+
+Logistic regression on a small set of hand-shaped features: linear x5 and x7, the interaction x0*x1, the
+squares x3^2 and x4^2, a periodic sin(2*x2) and |x6|. The other columns add only noise. Every term and
+shape was chosen by repeated 5-fold cross-validation on the training split.
 """
 import numpy as np
 
 
